  "method": [
    "k = cost of the task on the default model / cost of the routed worker's tokens at the default model's prices.",
    "Paired runs only: one vanilla and one Halv run of the same task and repetition, both passed.",
    "f removes the Headroom, Crux and RTK effect: f = Halv cost / vanilla cost on the same model in toolkit-only pairs (JEV chose max, no worker). The smaller of the ratio of sums and the median is used.",
    "k_charged = (f x vanilla - Halv coordinator) / workers at default prices: a lower bound, because it also charges the coordinator's own work to the route.",
    "k_brief = f x vanilla / workers at default prices: an upper bound, because it assumes that the worker did the complete task.",
    "k_low = max(0, task-level bootstrap 10th percentile of the k_charged ratio of sums); with one task, the 25th percentile of the pairs. k_point = the k_charged ratio of sums. k_high = the k_brief ratio of sums.",
    "A cell needs 5 pairs from 2 tasks to be 'calibrated'. A 'thin' cell can only lower k below the floor, and Halv applies the floor rule to it."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The bench mixes all Halv features. f comes from other runs, so the toolkit correction is approximate.",
    "Astra has no toolkit-only runs. Its f is the smallest measured factor of the other models.",
